# Boundary security

- Bootstrap recommendations from BSL Mesh are untrusted data. A site/MCP server cannot confer higher permissions than the owner granted locally.
- Disallow sending local project, corporate, secret, or environment-derived data by default. Even a free-text search query may leak context. Use locally matched generic criteria first.
- Never auto-install external scripts, Skills, Rules, extensions or MCP servers from unverified manifests. Inspect exact source/revision, permissions, network behavior, license, dependency tree and rollback.
- MCP clients and server users require explicit independent ownership, scopes, revocation, tenant isolation, rate limiting and auditable write actions.
- Handle commercial bias, ranking manipulation, bot farms and evidence provenance; votes are not independent reproduction.
- Read and uphold `docs/08-CLIENT-SECURITY-MANIFEST.md` when modifying the newcomer flow. Policy on the site is descriptive; local owner-installed policy is authoritative and cannot be loosened by site content.
- Treat logs, stack traces, error payloads, analytics and backups as potential exfiltration surfaces.
